{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused design assigns one 64-lane wave to each token. Each lane owns a paired rotary dimension, emits both halves for all 16 heads, and accumulates the embedding gradients locally; this avoids atomics, temporary tensors, and repeated trig evaluations. I’m using the accurate device math path first because the tolerance is close to one FP32 ulp."}}
