{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"agent_message","text":"The parallel reduction’s lane tree is `(lane0 + lane2) + (lane1 + lane3)`. By mapping the four PyTorch partial sums as `lane0=A0+A1`, `lane2=A2`, `lane1=A3`, `lane3=0`, that hardware tree becomes exactly `((A0+A1)+A2)+A3`. I’m testing this exact, head-parallel mapping now."}}
