{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"agent_message","text":"The large-shape bottleneck is the one-wave kernel’s 16 serial head steps. A two-wave exact tree can reduce the critical path to 12 steps: one wave forms `((A0+A1)+A2)`, the other forms `A3`, then their sum is precisely PyTorch’s order. I’m prototyping that as a third path; it keeps the same memory traffic."}}
